      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Take Sertraline and dextromethorphan together with caution, as they can both increase serotonin levels and potentially lead to a dangerous interaction known as serotonin syndrome. Do not use dextromethorphan alone as it does not treat the underlying cause of your productive cough; instead, consult a doctor to avoid suppressing the cough too early and worsening the infection. Since you have sleep issues, ask your physician immediately for guidance on safe over-the-counter options or prescription cough medicines that will not interfere with your depression treatment.",
